---
import Gallery from '../../layouts/Gallery.astro';
import Related from '../../components/Related.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');

---
<Gallery title="Pattern: field editor">
  <p class="demo-note">
    <strong>Master-data maintenance — the SM30 case.</strong> A back-office user opens one
    record and corrects a handful of fields: a name typo, a credit limit, a date. They do it
    a few times a week, not all day, and "done" means the whole record committed once, with
    each field given the input its type deserves — a date picker for a date, a currency field
    for money, a stepper for a count. One row per <em>field</em>, not one row per record, which is what
    makes this different from <a href={base + '/patterns/editable-grid'}>the editable grid</a>.
  </p>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>The screen</h2>
    <form method="post" action="/vendors/V-1001">
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-row-edit data-density="compact">
        <caption class="bo-visually-hidden">Vendor master data, one row per field</caption>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col" style="inline-size: 14rem">Field</th>
            <th scope="col">Value</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr data-row-id="name">
            <th scope="row">Vendor name<br /><span class="bo-u-text-muted" style="font-weight: 400">Legal entity as registered</span></th>
            <td><input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless" id="fe-name" aria-label="Vendor name" value="Umbrella Logistics GmbH" /></td>
          </tr>
          <tr data-row-id="incorporated">
            <th scope="row">Incorporated<br /><span class="bo-u-text-muted" style="font-weight: 400">Date of incorporation</span></th>
            <td><input class="bo-input bo-input--seamless" type="date" id="fe-date" aria-label="Incorporated" value="2011-04-18" /></td>
          </tr>
          <tr data-row-id="terms">
            <th scope="row">Payment terms<br /><span class="bo-u-text-muted" style="font-weight: 400">Net days</span></th>
            <td>
              <select class="bo-select bo-select--seamless" id="fe-terms" aria-label="Payment terms">
                <option>Net 14</option><option selected>Net 30</option><option>Net 60</option>
              </select>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr data-row-id="credit">
            <th scope="row">Credit limit<br /><span class="bo-u-text-muted" style="font-weight: 400">Per open order</span></th>
            <td>
              <div class="bo-money">
                <select class="bo-select bo-select--seamless bo-money__currency" aria-label="Currency">
                  <option selected>EUR</option><option>USD</option><option>JPY</option>
                </select>
                <input class="bo-input bo-input--numeric bo-input--seamless bo-money__amount" type="number" step="0.01" id="fe-credit" aria-label="Credit limit" value="250000.00" />
              </div>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr data-row-id="moq">
            <th scope="row">Minimum order<br /><span class="bo-u-text-muted" style="font-weight: 400">Units per line</span></th>
            <td>
              <div class="bo-quantity">
                <input class="bo-input bo-input--numeric bo-input--seamless bo-quantity__input" type="number" min="1" step="1" id="fe-moq" aria-label="Minimum order" value="24" />
                <span class="bo-quantity__unit">pcs</span>
              </div>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr data-row-id="active">
            <th scope="row">Active<br /><span class="bo-u-text-muted" style="font-weight: 400">Blocks new orders when off</span></th>
            <td><input class="bo-checkbox" type="checkbox" id="fe-active" aria-label="Active" checked /></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="bo-data-table__footer">
      <span class="bo-badge bo-badge--warning" data-any-dirty hidden>Unsaved changes</span>
      <button class="bo-btn bo-btn--secondary" type="reset">Cancel</button>
      <button class="bo-btn" type="submit">Save vendor</button>
    </div>
    </form>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">
      Edit any value: that row marks itself unsaved, and <strong>one Save at the bottom
      commits the record</strong>. Cancel is a native <code>type="reset"</code>, which
      restores every control to its default — including re-deriving the money field's
      precision — and <code>initRowEdit()</code> clears the unsaved marks with it.
    </p>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">
      <strong>Why one Save and not one per row.</strong> These rows are the FIELDS OF ONE
      RECORD, not a list of records. A Save per field means six requests for one logical
      edit, a Cancel that undoes a third of what the user changed, and — measured on the
      first version of this page — a button sitting <strong>228px from the field it saves</strong>
      in an actions column taking 37% of the table. Per-row Save belongs to
      <a href={base + '/patterns/editable-grid'}>the editable grid</a>, where each row really
      is a record.
    </p>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">
      <strong>Prefer saving on change?</strong> Use <code>data-row-edit="live"</code>: every
      committed change saves immediately and no buttons are needed. It suits settings-style
      screens where fields are independent and there is nothing to cancel as a set — but you
      owe the user per-field success and failure feedback, which the batch form gets for free
      from one response.
    </p>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">
      <strong>Zero new CSS.</strong> This screen is
      <a href={base + '/components/data-table'}>the data table</a> with
      <code>data-row-edit</code>, and the value cells are the ordinary typed inputs —
      <a href={base + '/components/money'}>money</a>,
      <a href={base + '/components/quantity'}>quantity</a>, a native date input, a select and a
      checkbox. Nothing here is a "field editor component", and there is deliberately no such
      class to learn.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Anatomy</h2>
    <ol class="bo-stack bo-stack--tight docs-list">
      <li><strong>Field column</strong> — a <code>&lt;th scope="row"&gt;</code>, not a
        <code>&lt;td&gt;</code>: the field name labels its row, which is what lets a screen
        reader announce "Credit limit" when the value cell takes focus.</li>
      <li><strong>Value column</strong> — one control per data type, from
        <a href={base + '/components/form'}>the form primitives</a>. Seamless variants
        (<code>--seamless</code>) on <em>every</em> field, including the money and quantity
        ones — a screen where three fields read as text and two read as boxes tells the user
        the boxed ones are editable and the others are not, which is exactly backwards.</li>
      <li><strong>Row actions</strong> — the dirty badge plus Save/Cancel that
        <code>initRowEdit()</code> reveals, in
        <code>.bo-data-table__row-edit-actions</code>.</li>
      <li><strong>Hint text</strong> — one muted line under the field name. It belongs in the
        field column, never as placeholder text in the input, which
        <a href={base + '/concepts/accessibility'}>disappears the moment someone types</a>.</li>
    </ol>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Data contract</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Request</th><th scope="col">Returns / on failure</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="bo-data-table__col--code">GET /vendors/:id/fields</td>
            <td>the full field list; every row renders even if the user may not edit it</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="bo-data-table__col--code">PATCH /vendors/:id</td>
            <td><strong>one field per request</strong>, keyed by <code>data-row-id</code>. Returns the
              re-rendered <code>&lt;tr&gt;</code> so the server owns formatting — a credit limit comes
              back as <code>250,000.00</code>, not as whatever was typed</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="bo-data-table__col--code">422 (validation)</td>
            <td>the same <code>&lt;tr&gt;</code> with <code>data-row-state="error"</code> and the message in
              the row. <strong>Swap it in yourself</strong> — htmx discards non-2xx bodies by
              default, so a 422 that is not opted in via <code>htmx-ext-response-targets</code>
              changes nothing on screen</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="bo-data-table__col--code">409 (conflict)</td>
            <td>someone else changed this field first. Return the current value and let the user
              choose — see <a href={base + '/concepts/concurrency'}>concurrency</a></td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted">
      One field per request is the point: a whole-record PUT makes two people editing two
      different fields overwrite each other, and it is exactly the case this screen exists for.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>States</h2>
    <div class="bo-data-table-container" tabindex="0">
      <table class="bo-data-table" data-density="compact">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">State</th><th scope="col">What ships</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>Loading</td><td>skeleton rows — the field list is known before the values are, so the labels can render first</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Saving a row</td><td><code>aria-busy</code> on that row only; every other row stays editable</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Validation error</td><td><code>data-row-state="error"</code> on the row, message in the row, value left as typed so the user can fix rather than retype</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Read-only field</td><td>render the value as text, not a disabled input — a disabled control tells the user nothing about <em>why</em>. See <a href={base + '/concepts/permissions'}>permissions</a></td></tr>
          <tr><td>No permission at all</td><td>omit the screen, not the buttons</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Conflict</td><td>409 row swap showing the other value, with an explicit choice; nothing auto-merges</td></tr>
          <tr><td>Empty</td><td>does not occur — a record with no fields is a bug, not a state</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="demo">
    <h2>Components used</h2>
    <p class="bo-u-text-muted"><span class="bo-badge">complexity 3 of 4</span></p>
    <ul class="bo-cluster docs-list-bare">
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/data-table'}>Data table</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/inline-editing'}>Inline editing</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/form'}>Form controls</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/money'}>Money</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/quantity'}>Quantity</a></li>
      <li><a class="bo-badge bo-badge--type" href={base + '/components/badge'}>Badge</a></li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <script>
    import { initRowEdit, initMoneyField, initQuantity } from '@busy-office/ui/js';
    initRowEdit();
    initMoneyField();
    initQuantity();

    /* The framework marks each ROW dirty; aggregating that into one
       "unsaved changes" badge is application state, so it lives here rather
       than in the framework. Three lines, and it is the honest split. */
    const table = document.querySelector('table[data-row-edit]');
    const badge = document.querySelector('[data-any-dirty]');
    const sync = () => { badge.hidden = !table.querySelector('tr[data-row-state="dirty"]'); };
    document.addEventListener('input', sync);
    document.addEventListener('change', sync);
    document.addEventListener('reset', () => setTimeout(sync, 0));
  </script>

  <Related links={[
    ["/components/inline-editing", "Inline editing"],
    ["/patterns/editable-grid", "Editable grid"],
    ["/patterns/record-detail", "Record detail"],
    ["/concepts/concurrency", "Concurrency & conflicts"],
  ]} />
</Gallery>
